course: dictionary
lesson: 9528
title: Stingy and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Stingy is an informal word, so you will hear it in talk and stories more than in formal writing. It means not willing to spend or share money, food or things. When Kieran says, «Sorry, I need it today», he is refusing to share, so the context shows he is being stingy.
explain: Stingy has a second meaning too: small in amount. A «stingy portion» is a small helping of food. To choose the right meaning, look at the words around it. Is the word describing a person, or how much there is?
explain: People sometimes choose a kinder word to hide the real feeling. «Careful with money» is a polite cover for stingy. Deano calls Kieran «tight», which is slang and much blunter, so context also tells you how strong the word is.
fact: Stingy is an adjective: stingy, stingier, stingiest.
fact: «Stingy» means not willing to spend or share money, food or things.
fact: «Stingy» can also mean small in amount, as in «a stingy portion».
fact: «Careful with money» is a polite way to say stingy.
fact: «Tight» is informal slang for stingy, and «well tight» means really stingy.
exercise: Kieran says, «Sorry, I need it today.» Why is this stingy? | *He won't share what he has | He gives away everything he owns | He is too busy to speak | He is very kind to everyone
exercise: «A stingy portion» is a portion that is | Hot and fresh | Sweet and sticky | Huge and filling | *Small in amount
exercise: Which word is an informal word for stingy? | *Tight | Generous | Kindly | Patient
test: Stingy is an adjective. Which is its comparative form? | stinging | stingy | *stingier | stingiest
test: «Careful with money» is a polite cover for which word? | Loud | Generous | Glad | *Stingy
exam: «The shop gave a stingy portion of chips.» What does stingy mean here? | *Small in amount | Hot and fresh | Shiny | Giving away lots
